    "tree": {
      "sha": "d7ca4ee152099161435613ae2ae6209e7ec8973a",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/jphacks/tkb_2615/git/trees/d7ca4ee152099161435613ae2ae6209e7ec8973a"
    },
    "message": "Call the runtime model first in the live model check\n\nUsageLedger keeps calls free for the analysis when it reserves a runtime\ncall, so on the check's 3-call account the Haiku runtime call, made\nlast after Opus and Sonnet, was always denied before any request\n(#148). The check now calls runtime first, under the same caps. The\nsettings, ledger and tasks move into the live_model_check fixture, and\ntests/unit/llm/test_accounting.py runs that case with a fake provider,\nso a ledger rule that denies one of its calls fails the offline suite.\nWith the old order that test fails the way the live run did.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
